# Requisições das 10 rotas da Api contra o ambiente local (docker compose up).
# Roda no Visual Studio 2022 (17.12 ou mais novo) e no REST Client do VS Code: só variáveis, `# @name`,
# `{{nome.response.body.$.campo}}` e `{{$guid}}`. Envie primeiro as requisições de token; as seguintes
# leem o token e os ids das respostas anteriores. Tokens expiram em minutos: reenvie a requisição de token.
# Contrato completo: openapi-v1.json, ao lado deste arquivo.

@api = http://localhost:8080
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ledger/protocol/openid-connect/token
@ana = 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111

### Token do backoffice: contas, limite, estorno, cadastro e leituras
# @name backoffice
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=backoffice&client_secret=backoffice_dev

### Token do compliance: dados pessoais completos e leituras de posição
# @name compliance
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=compliance&client_secret=compliance_dev

### Token do payments-hub: créditos
# @name paymentsHub
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=payments-hub&client_secret=payments-hub_dev

### Modo delegado, passo 1: a ana entra no channel-web por senha (só neste realm local)
# @name anaLogin
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=channel-web&username=ana&password=ana_dev

### Modo delegado, passo 2: o channel-app troca o token da ana por um destinado à Api
# @name channelApp
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange&client_id=channel-app&client_secret=channel-app_dev&subject_token_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:access_token&subject_token={{anaLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}&audience=ledger-api

### Abre uma conta para a ana
# @name openAccount
POST {{api}}/v1/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{backoffice.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "customerId": "{{ana}}"
}

### Troca o limite de crédito da conta
PUT {{api}}/v1/accounts/{{openAccount.response.body.$.id}}/credit-limit
Authorization: Bearer {{backoffice.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "creditLimit": "500.00"
}

### Credita R$ 150,75
# @name credit
POST {{api}}/v1/accounts/{{openAccount.response.body.$.id}}/credits
Authorization: Bearer {{paymentsHub.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "amount": "150.75",
  "category": "PIX_IN",
  "externalReference": "credito-{{$guid}}"
}

### Debita R$ 40,00 em nome da ana (modo delegado)
POST {{api}}/v1/accounts/{{openAccount.response.body.$.id}}/debits
Authorization: Bearer {{channelApp.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "amount": "40.00",
  "category": "PIX_OUT",
  "externalReference": "debito-{{$guid}}"
}

### Estorna o crédito
POST {{api}}/v1/accounts/{{openAccount.response.body.$.id}}/entries/{{credit.response.body.$.id}}/reversal
Authorization: Bearer {{backoffice.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "externalReference": "estorno-{{$guid}}"
}

### Saldo atual
GET {{api}}/v1/accounts/{{openAccount.response.body.$.id}}/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{backoffice.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Saldo em um momento, pela ana (modo delegado); `at` nunca no futuro
GET {{api}}/v1/accounts/{{openAccount.response.body.$.id}}/balance?at=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{channelApp.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Extrato, primeira página; a seguinte vem com `cursor` igual ao `nextCursor` recebido
GET {{api}}/v1/accounts/{{openAccount.response.body.$.id}}/statement?limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{compliance.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Cadastra um cliente; um CPF já cadastrado responde 409 cpf-already-registered
# @name registerCustomer
POST {{api}}/v1/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{backoffice.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "name": "Carla Dias",
  "cpf": "390.533.447-05",
  "birthDate": "1988-07-21",
  "email": "carla@ledger.local"
}

### Cliente mascarado
GET {{api}}/v1/customers/{{registerCustomer.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{backoffice.response.body.$.access_token}}

### A própria ana, mascarada (modo delegado: outro cliente responde 404)
GET {{api}}/v1/customers/{{ana}}
Authorization: Bearer {{channelApp.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Dados pessoais completos
GET {{api}}/v1/customers/{{registerCustomer.response.body.$.id}}/personal-data
Authorization: Bearer {{compliance.response.body.$.access_token}}
